\ Compare exact wide counters against the six existing short day vectors.
\ This exercises the native-to-wide adapter and every wide counter
\ using values already established independently by the original
\ short source-level examples.

\ Pass the already-declared signed result record to CAL's conversion.
\ Using 'a wide signed day' twice in one routine declares the same local
\ name twice, which CAL-4018 rejects. The conversion also publishes its
\ result in 'the converted signed day result', used immediately below.
\ The comparison uses the global example and wide calendar example;
\ its old 'a native calendar question' parameter was never referenced.
\ Calling it repeatedly declared the same unused local six times.
\ Diagnostic-only failure witness for the first native/wide count mismatch.
\ This does not alter expected counts, arithmetic, or the passing path.
\ The CAL-4018 implicit local 'string' is used at most once per routine.
The comparison wide day text is a string.

To report native and wide calculation count discrepancy:
  Put "Native/wide calculation count discrepancy; native_count=" into the check report.
  Convert the example's calculation count to a string.
  Append the string to the check report.
  Append "; wide_count=" to the check report.
  Append the wide calendar example's calculation count to the check report.
  Append "; native_c=" to the check report.
  Report native calculation coordinate.
  Append "; wide_c=" to the check report.
  Spell the wide calendar example's calculation day into the comparison wide day text.
  Append the comparison wide day text to the check report.
  Append "; native_t=" to the check report.
  Report native requested coordinate.
  Append "; wide_t=" to the check report.
  Spell the wide calendar example's requested day into the comparison wide day text.
  Append the comparison wide day text to the check report.

To report native calculation coordinate:
  Convert the example's calculation day to a string.
  Append the string to the check report.

To report native requested coordinate:
  Convert the example's requested day to a string.
  Append the string to the check report.

To compare native and wide counters:
  Answer the example.
  Convert the example's calculation day into the converted signed day result.
  If the native widening succeeded is not 1,
    put "Conversion of the native calculation day failed." into the check report; exit.
  Put the converted signed day result into the wide calendar example's calculation day.
  Convert the example's requested day into the converted signed day result.
  If the native widening succeeded is not 1,
    put "Conversion of the native requested day failed." into the check report; exit.
  Put the converted signed day result into the wide calendar example's requested day.
  Answer the wide calendar example.
  Convert the example's calculation count to a string.
  If the wide calendar example's calculation count is not the string,
    report native and wide calculation count discrepancy; exit.
  Convert the example's requested count to the string.
  If the wide calendar example's requested count is not the string,
    put "Wide and native requested counts disagree." into the check report; exit.
  Convert the example's day distance to the string.
  If the wide calendar example's day distance is not the string,
    put "Wide and native inclusive day distances disagree." into the check report; exit.
  Convert the example's day sum to the string.
  If the wide calendar example's day sum is not the string,
    put "Wide and native counter sums disagree." into the check report; exit.
  If the wide calendar example's day direction is not the example's day direction,
    put "Wide and native directions disagree." into the check report; exit.

